# Homebrew tap setup

This folder is a **reference bundle**, rendered here for convenience — it is
not consumed by {{github_repo_name}} itself. Copy its contents into your
`{{github_user}}/homebrew-tap` repository to receive automated Homebrew
{% if primary_executable %}cask{% else %}formula{% endif %} bumps on every release.

## How it works

On each release, this project's `bump-homebrew` job (in `release.yml`) sends a
`repository_dispatch` event to `{{github_user}}/homebrew-tap`. The listener
workflow in this folder receives that event, resolves the new version, bumps
the {% if primary_executable %}cask{% else %}formula{% endif %}, audits it, and opens a pull request against the tap —
all inside the tap repository, using the tap's own `GITHUB_TOKEN`.

## One-time tap setup

1. Create the tap repository:

   ```sh
   gh repo create {{github_user}}/homebrew-tap --public \
     --description "Homebrew tap for {{github_user}} packages"
   ```

2. Clone the tap locally and `cd` into it — the bootstrap commands below
   operate on files inside this checkout:

   ```sh
   gh repo clone {{github_user}}/homebrew-tap
   cd homebrew-tap
   ```

3. Bootstrap the initial {% if primary_executable %}cask{% else %}formula{% endif %}:
{% if primary_executable %}
   ```sh
   brew create --cask <github-release-asset-url>
   ```

   Then edit the generated `Casks/{{github_repo_name}}.rb` (written inside
   this clone) to fill in the `sha256`, `url`, and `version` stanzas for your
   release artifact.
{% else %}
   ```sh
   brew tap-new {{github_user}}/tap
   brew create --set-name {{github_repo_name}} <pypi-sdist-url>
   brew update-python-resources {{github_user}}/tap/{{github_repo_name}}
   ```

   `brew create`/`update-python-resources` write into `Formula/{{github_repo_name}}.rb`
   inside this clone; `update-python-resources` fills in the Python `resource`
   blocks for the formula's dependencies.
{% endif %}
4. Commit the listener workflow from this folder,
   `update-{% if primary_executable %}cask{% else %}formula{% endif %}-dispatch.yml`, to the tap's
   `.github/workflows/` directory.

## Token setup (in this project's repo)

In **this** project's repository — `{{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}` — add
a fine-grained personal access token as the `HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN` secret, scoped
to `{{github_user}}/homebrew-tap` with **Contents: write** permission only.
That is all the `POST /dispatches` API requires; the tap opens its own pull
request with its own `GITHUB_TOKEN`, so **Pull requests: write** is not needed
on the PAT.

```sh
gh secret set HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN --repo {{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}
```

When `HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN` is unset, the `bump-homebrew` job skips with a
notice — it never fails the release.

